schema 1

// Desktop profile for the direct-scanout probe.
//
// Passed explicitly so the probe is hermetic. Without it the session discovers
// whatever desktop profile the operator has installed, which may enable a
// shell or bind session operations this one-application fixture cannot supply.
// The fixture must be independent of the operator's desktop configuration.
//
// The core configuration is passed for the same reason and is separate:
// `--config` and `--no-config` are mutually exclusive, so a probe that needs a
// core config cannot also fall back to the compiled desktop profile.
//
// The shell is off: there is no shell process, and `session:window-switcher`
// would name a capability this session does not have.
//
// Nothing is bound. A session with no window manager registers no shortcuts at
// all -- they are resolved against a policy client's configuration and there is
// no policy client here -- so a binding would describe something that cannot
// happen. The probe's client exits on its own; that is the exit.
shell { enabled #false; }
shortcut {
  profile "direct-scanout-standalone"
}
